Around the beginning of May I downloaded slash'em, having played only 
nethack before.  In order to get a feeling of the new game or to 'learn' 
it, I started, successively, three games and switched to explore mode 
after the first (few) move(s).  (Did not want the wand of wishing.) I 
chose a flame mage, an ice mage and a lycanthrope, all character classes 
that I had never played before.

All of them seemed very difficult to me, in particular the lycanthrope. 
  For the mages, things became much easier when I finally realized that 
to cope with the overpowered nature of slash'em one should counter with 
something equally overpowered - using the engraving of "Elbereth".  I 
switched back to my old mode of playing wizards (in NH3.1.3), using the 
athame deliberately to save my skin.  Naturally, one has to survive till 
one gets an athame by sacrificing but this happened pretty early for 
both mages.  (Of course, they died a lot before and still occasionally 
after, but then I am only in the learning phase now.)  I expected to 
have "ascended" the flame mage by now.  But despite of explore mode, you 
can "lose" the game; it crashed by a bug when my mage, appropriately 
named "buggy" moved up a staircase.  (The message was "oops" and 
something.)  Afterwards I made the mistake of using recover instead of 
just switching to the backup copy.  Recover produced a save file, but 
each time I fire the game up, it just pops up a window for a split 
second and is gone again.  (If anyone is interested, I can send them the 
save file.  I am playing on a Windows XP system, and I believe my 
version of slash'em is the newest one available.  With nethack I did not 
have any crashes on XP, only in the past on Linux systems.  But there 
recover always worked properly.)

However, I am writing this because of the other game, my Ice mage who 
has in the meantime explored the dungeon down to level 35.

He is lawful and got, by sacrificing, some pretty cool pets (much better 
than the shadow wolves and minions that the chaotic flame mage had had). 
These were two movanic and two monadic devas.  They are pretty scary, 
considering the number of attacks they get, the fact that rarely 
anything is able to harm them and their levels and hit points are both 
much higher than those of my mage.  So I have to make sure none of them 
will go wild (still hope they will get peaceful at worst).  One of the 
movanic devas was killed in a battle with many nasties, so I can 
understand this.  But something curious happened to one of the monadic 
devas.  I went back to Grund's stronghold (on Dlvl 13, IIRC) to read 
again a spellbook of acid stream that I had left there, after having 
forgotten the spell.  So the stronghold was already cleaned out.  One of 
the monadic devas, the movanic deva and a pit bull ('Pit') accompanied 
me.  (Why does the game not accept my giving a name to the monadic deva, 
b.t.w.?)  While I went to get and read the book (which I took along this 
time), my pets strayed around.  When I went back and was near the exit, 
I suddenly got the message "you have a sad feeling, then it passes".  I 
used my magic whistle immediately.  It was the monadic deva that had 
died!  I blinded myself but did not see any dangerous monster on the 
level.  Of course, I did not go back to check for any nonthinking 
monsters, for whatever can kill my monadic deva can also kill me...  I 
think it is likely to have been a single monster, since the level was 
almost empty.  But what monster with a level not exceeding  13 (my 
character level was 12 or 13 and the dungeon level 13) can kill a 
monadic deva?  They seemed almost invincible to me...   Any ideas?
